What the agent-action tools need from the server (hermes' camofox plugin,
../hermes-camofox-plugin/action-feedback.patch).

- POST /tabs/:tabId/click takes `text` (with `exact`, `nth`) besides ref and
  selector: the visible element showing that text (Playwright getByText,
  visible only), in the page first, then its frames. More than one match
  without nth, or none, is a 422 text_not_matched that lists the matches.
- POST /tabs/:tabId/wait takes `text`: polls (250 ms) until the text is
  visible in the page or a frame, at most `timeout` (cap 60 s); answers
  found and waitedMs.
- POST /tabs/:tabId/evaluate: a navigation that destroyed the page's
  context is a 409 navigation_race saying so (the expression's click
  probably worked), an error thrown by the expression a 400 script_error
  with its first line; both were "Internal server error".
- In production, a 4xx error (stale ref, element not actionable, bad
  selector, no text match) carries its first line instead of "Internal
  server error"; 5xx stay opaque.
Not upstream.

